  "title": "An explicit formal quotient for Class 214 inversion sequences",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For each n>=0, let I_n consist of tuples (e_1,...,e_n) with 0<=e_i<i and with no i<j<k satisfying e_i>=e_k and e_j>=e_k; the empty tuple is counted once. Put F(z)=sum_{n>=0}|I_n|z^n. In formal series at z=0 define X=(1-2z-sqrt(1-4z))/(2z), with sqrt(1-4z)=1+O(z); q=X^2/(1+2X); b=X^3/((1+X)(1+2X)); H(u)=z(1+u)^2-u; R0(u)=-zu^2(1-z-zu)/(1-zu); R1(u)=u^2(1-z-zu)^2/(1-zu). For every j>=0 define t_j=z^j q/(1-q sum_{r=1}^j z^r), with the empty sum zero, and D_j=product_{i=0}^j H(t_i). Then A=sum_{j>=0}R0(t_j)/D_j and L=q+sum_{j>=0}R1(t_j)/D_j converge z-adically in Z[[z]], their summands having exact orders j+4 and j+3 respectively, and F=(b-A)/(zL). Here L=z^2+O(z^3) and b-A=z^3+O(z^4), so the quotient is well-defined. If A_m,L_m retain exactly j=0,...,m-1 and F_m=(b-A_m)/(zL_m), then for every integer m>=0, F_m belongs to Q(z,X) intersect Z[[z]] and F_m-F=z^(m+3)+O(z^(m+4)). This solves the explicit generating-function representation part only; no algebraicity, transcendence, analytic continuation, or asymptotic assertion is made.",
